\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 \ul \ulc0 \
\
Decision Tree:
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\
A decision tree is a supervised learning algorithm used for both classification and regression tasks. It has a hierarchical tree structure which consists \
of a root node, branches, internal nodes and leaf nodes. It works like a flowchart that helps in making step-by-step decisions, \
\
where:\
Root node is starting node\
Internal nodes represent attribute tests\
Branches represent attribute values\
Leaf nodes represent final decisions or predictions.\
\

\f0\b \ul Pruning Techniques:
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\

\f0\b \ul 1. Post Pruning :
\f1\b0 \ulnone  Post-pruning is a pruning strategy in which the decision tree is allowed to grow to its full depth first, after which unnecessary or weak \
branches are removed. Unlike pre-pruning, this approach does not restrict the tree during training. Instead, it analyzes the fully grown tree and \
evaluates whether certain subtrees contribute meaningfully to predictive performance.\
\

\f0\b \ul 2. Pre Pruning:
\f1\b0 \ulnone  Pre-pruning is also known as early stopping, is a pruning strategy in which the growth of the decision tree is restricted during the training phase itself. \
Instead of allowing the tree to grow fully and then trimming it later, pre-pruning prevents certain splits from being created if they do not satisfy \
predefined constraints.\
\
\

\f0\b \ul Entropy
\f1\b0 \ulnone : It is the measure of uncertainty of a random variable, it characterizes the impurity of collection of examples. The higher the entropy more the \
information content.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Example: if a dataset has an equal number of "Yes" and "No" outcomes (like 3 people who bought a product and 3 who didn\'92t), the entropy is high because it\'92s uncertain \
which outcome to predict. But if all the outcomes are the same (all "Yes" or all "No") the entropy is 0 meaning there is no uncertainty left in predicting the outcome\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \

\f0\b \ul Information Gain: 
\f1\b0 \ulnone  Information Gain tells us how useful a feature is for splitting data into groups. It measures how much the uncertainty/entropy/randomness decreases \
after the split. A good feature/variable will create clearer groups and the feature with the highest Information Gain is chosen to make the decision.\
\

\f0\b \ul Gini Index/Impurity:\

\f1\b0 \ulnone \
It is calculated by summing the squared probabilities of each outcome in a distribution and subtracting the result from 1.\
A lower Gini Index indicates a more homogeneous or pure distribution while a higher Gini Index indicates a more heterogeneous or impure distribution.\
\
\

\f0\b \ul Algorithms:
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\

\f0\b \ul 1. ID3:
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}ID3 is a decision tree learning algorithm used for solving classification problems. It builds the tree using a top-down, greedy approach by selecting the attribute that \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8259 	}          provides the highest Information Gain which is calculated using entropy.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}ID3 mainly works with categorical attributes and recursively splits the data until the nodes become pure or no attributes remain.\
\ls1\ilvl0{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}It is simple and easy to interpret but can overfit the training data and does not handle continuous features directly.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\

\f0\b \ul 2. C4.5:
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}C4.5 is an improved extension of the ID3 algorithm. It is designed to overcome several limitations of ID3, such as handling continuous attributes, managing missing values \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li1440\fi-1440\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 	and reducing bias toward attributes with many values by using Gain Ratio instead of Information Gain.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Uses Gain Ratio as the splitting criterion to reduce bias toward attributes with many distinct values.\
\ls2\ilvl0{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Can handle both categorical and continuous attributes, making it more flexible than ID3.\
\ls2\ilvl0{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Applies post-pruning techniques to simplify the tree and reduce overfitting.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\

\f0\b \ul 3. CART (Classification and Regression Trees):
\f1\b0 \ulnone \
\
\pard\tx220\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\li720\fi-720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}CART is a widely used decision tree algorithm that can handle both classification and regression problems. CART builds binary decision trees by repeatedly splitting the \
\ls3\ilvl0	       dataset into two subsets based on the most informative feature.\
\ls3\ilvl0{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Works for both classification and regression tasks.\
\ls3\ilvl0{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Uses Gini Impurity for classification and variance reduction for regression.\
\ls3\ilvl0{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Always produces binary trees, meaning each internal node splits into exactly two child nodes.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\
